# Phase 2 quotation hard-failure surface (D-15, QC-07)

`QAI_DATA_DIR` points the real `qai` binary at a fresh temp database (set by the
harness). `qai quran verify-quotation` is read-only: it verifies an externally
supplied quotation against the pinned `slug@version` and reports the verdict
together with the RESOLVED canonical hash. A mismatch is a hard failure — a
non-zero exit with a typed `QAI-QUR-*` code — never a success.

```console
$ qai db migrate
migrations applied; schema version [..]

```

```console
$ qai quran import ../../fixtures/quran/test-edition-min/manifest.json
imported test-edition-min@0.1.0 to Staged
note: synthetic test data — non-canonical (ADR-0101 fallback)

```

```console
$ qai quran activate test-edition-min@0.1.0 --yes
activated test-edition-min@0.1.0 (generation 1)

```

An exact quotation verifies (exit 0) with the stored canonical hash on the
pinned reference.

```console
$ qai quran verify-quotation --edition test-edition-min@0.1.0 --surah 1 --ayah 1 --text 'أوَيت تَساكُن كن لهُم ثُشأوَ'
verdict: ExactMatch
  text_hash: sha256:2c656d34d59038eed42464f08e753d2d6d16f702f09b8b05789abcaae792ba31
  reference: quran:test-edition-min@0.1.0:1:1

```

A tampered quotation is a hard failure: exit 3 with a typed code and the first
difference, never a success envelope or a synthesized hash.

```console
$ qai quran verify-quotation --edition test-edition-min@0.1.0 --surah 1 --ayah 1 --text 'tampered text'
? 3
error: quotation does not match canonical text (first difference at 0, expected 2c656d34d59038eed42464f08e753d2d6d16f702f09b8b05789abcaae792ba31)

```

A pinned edition that is not active is not-found (exit 5).

```console
$ qai quran verify-quotation --edition nope@0.1.0 --surah 1 --ayah 1 --text 'x'
? 5
error: citation edition not found

```
